### Core flow in one diagram

```text
                         ┌──────────────┐
                         │  EMPLOYEES   │
                         └──────┬───────┘
                                │
              ┌─────────────────┼──────────────────┐
              ▼                 ▼                  ▼
         CONTRACTS          ATTENDANCE        TIME OFF
              │                                  │
       ┌──────┼──────┐                    ┌──────┴──────┐
       ▼      ▼      ▼                    ▼             ▼
   POSITION  DEPT  SCHEDULE             TYPE       ALLOCATION
                         │                              │
                         ▼                              ▼
                  SCHEDULE DAYS                    REQUEST


              CONTRACT
                 │
                 ▼
        SALARY STRUCTURE
                 │
                 ▼
        STRUCTURE_RULES
                 │
                 ▼
           SALARY RULES
                 │
                 ▼
              PAYRUN
                 │
          ┌──────┴──────┐
          ▼             ▼
      PAYSLIP        PAYSLIP
          │
          ▼
    PAYSLIP_LINES
```

**One architectural correction I'd make before you start coding:** `department_id`, `working_schedule_id`, and similar employment attributes should have a deliberate ownership decision. If they are contract-specific terms, keep them on `contracts`; if they're immutable organizational relationships, reference them elsewhere. For your hackathon, keeping them on `contracts` is defensible because it preserves the employee's historical employment context.
